{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-phone-native-b-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-3","surface":"phone","area":"phone/native","refs":["F-phone-1206","F-phone-1207","F-phone-1213"],"severity":"S3","title":"A set ticked from the notification with the app closed can go unsaved with no word","what":"When the member taps Done on the workout notification and the phone cannot tick the set by itself, a note says 'Open MettleUp to save your set. Open it within 10 min'. The note then disappears by itself after 10 minutes. If the member opens the app later, the tap is quietly ignored: the set stays unticked and nothing says the tap was too late. The same happens to a set the phone ticked by itself with the app closed if the workout changed before the app took it: the card had already moved on as if the set was saved.","expected":"When a tapped set could not be saved, the app says so the next time it opens ('Your set from the notification was not saved, tick it here'), and points at the set.","evidence":["apps/mobile/modules/forge-rest/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/rest/RestCard.kt:816-820","apps/mobile/modules/forge-rest/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/rest/RestCard.kt:843-845","apps/mobile/modules/forge-rest/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/rest/RestActionReceiver.kt:47-57","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restDone.ts:285","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restDoneRun.ts:127-130","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restDone.ts:252-256","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restDoneRun.ts:89-100"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"late-done-tap-dropped-silently","who":"members","how_often":"sometimes: a member who taps Done with the app closed and opens it more than 10 minutes later","fix_line":"Keep a missed tap and tell the member about it when the app opens","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-phone-native-b-02","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-4","surface":"phone","area":"phone/native","refs":["F-phone-1224","FN-B-run-phone-native-b-01"],"severity":"S3","title":"A workout deleted in MettleUp can stay in Health Connect for good, with no retry and no word","what":"Deleting a workout in MettleUp asks Health Connect to remove its copy once. If Health Connect refuses or the call fails, only a hidden log line is written. Unlike a workout that failed to send (which waits on a 'Send again' list), nothing tries the removal again and the Health Connect page says nothing. Google Fit, Samsung Health and other apps reading Health Connect keep counting a workout and its calories that the member removed in MettleUp, so the two places disagree.","expected":"A removal that did not go through waits on a list and is tried again, and the Health Connect page says 'N deleted workouts are still in Health Connect, Remove again'.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/phone/healthConnect.ts:683-700","apps/mobile/src/tracker/phone/phonePrefs.ts:23-27","apps/mobile/src/tracker/phone/healthConnect.ts:585"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"health-delete-no-retry-list","who":"members","how_often":"rare: when Health Connect refuses or fails a delete","fix_line":"Keep failed removals on a list, retry them and show a Remove again line","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
